<div class="intro"><b>Please read before using our services.</b> These policies are intended to cover the NEWSKERALA.NET website, mobile applications published by or for NEWSKERALA.NET, and its official Telegram bot/channel. Some features may have additional notices. The final text must accurately reflect the services and third-party tools actually enabled.</div>
<section class="section" id="privacy"><h2><span class="num">01</span>Privacy Policy</h2><p>NEWSKERALA.NET (“we”, “us” or “our”) respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains what information may be collected, why it is used, when it may be shared and the choices available to you when you use our website, applications or Telegram services.</p>
<h3>Information you provide</h3><ul><li>Contact details and messages you submit through forms, email, feedback or support.</li><li>Information you choose to provide when creating an account, commenting, subscribing or using interactive features, if those features are available.</li><li>Messages or commands you send to our Telegram bot.</li></ul>
<h3>Information collected automatically</h3><ul><li>Technical details such as IP address, browser or app version, device type, operating system, language and timestamps.</li><li>Pages, articles or app screens viewed, links clicked, referring pages and general usage events.</li><li>Cookies, local storage, diagnostic logs and similar technologies, where used.</li></ul>
<h3>How we use information</h3><ul><li>Operate, maintain and secure the website, apps and Telegram services.</li><li>Deliver news alerts, requested subscriptions and service messages.</li><li>Respond to enquiries, feedback and support requests.</li><li>Understand service performance, fix errors and improve content and usability.</li><li>Detect spam, abuse, fraud or security incidents and comply with legal obligations.</li><li>Show advertising, measure campaigns or personalize content only where the relevant services are enabled and permitted.</li></ul>
<h3>Legal basis and consent</h3><p>Where applicable law requires a lawful basis or consent, we will process personal data on the appropriate basis and provide a way to withdraw consent where required. The specific basis may depend on the feature you use and the purpose of processing.</p>
<h3>Sharing and service providers</h3><p>We do not sell personal information. We may share limited information with hosting providers, security vendors, analytics providers, advertising partners, app distribution platforms, Telegram and other service providers where needed to operate the services. We may also disclose information where required by law, valid legal process, or to protect users and our rights. Service providers may process information under their own terms and privacy notices.</p>
<h3>Retention and security</h3><p>We keep information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described, including security, dispute resolution and legal compliance. We use reasonable technical and organizational safeguards, but no internet transmission or storage system can be guaranteed completely secure.</p>
<h3>Children's privacy</h3><p>Our services are intended for a general audience and are not knowingly designed to collect personal data from children in violation of applicable law. A parent or guardian may contact us if they believe a child has provided personal information.</p>
<h3>International processing and external links</h3><p>Some service providers may process information in countries other than your own. External websites and embedded content are governed by their respective privacy policies; please review those policies before providing information.</p></section>
<section class="section" id="apps"><h2><span class="num">02</span>Mobile Applications</h2><p>This section applies to mobile applications branded, published or operated by NEWSKERALA.NET. App-specific features and permissions may differ.</p><div class="grid"><div class="tile"><b>Device permissions</b><span>An app may request permissions such as notifications, network access, camera, photos or storage only when a feature needs them. You can manage permissions in your device settings.</span></div><div class="tile"><b>Notifications</b><span>If enabled, push notifications may be used for breaking news, headlines or service notices. You can turn them off through app or device settings.</span></div><div class="tile"><b>Diagnostics</b><span>Crash reports and performance information may be processed to troubleshoot problems, if diagnostic tools are integrated.</span></div><div class="tile"><b>Third-party SDKs</b><span>Analytics, advertising, login, push notification or crash-reporting SDKs may have their own data practices. Their actual use must be disclosed in the relevant app-store listing.</span></div></div><p>We do not claim that every app collects all categories listed here. The permissions, SDKs, account features and data collection for each published app must be checked and described accurately in that app's store listing and in-app disclosures.</p></section>
<section class="section" id="telegram"><h2><span class="num">03</span>Telegram Bot &amp; Channel</h2><p>When you interact with our Telegram bot or join our Telegram channel, Telegram may make certain account and message information available to the bot or platform, depending on your settings and the interaction. This can include a Telegram user identifier, public username, display name, messages and commands sent to the bot.</p><ul><li>We use bot interactions to respond to commands, deliver requested news updates and maintain the service.</li><li>Joining a public channel may expose your membership or activity according to Telegram's features and privacy settings.</li><li>Blocking the bot or using an available stop command prevents future bot messages but may not erase information already retained in logs or backups.</li><li>Telegram independently processes information under its own privacy policy and terms.</li></ul><p>Telegram privacy information: <a href="https://telegram.org/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">telegram.org/privacy</a>.</p></section>
<section class="section" id="terms"><h2><span class="num">04</span>Terms of Use</h2><p>By accessing NEWSKERALA.NET, its applications or Telegram services, you agree to use them lawfully and responsibly. If you do not agree with these terms, please discontinue use.</p><h3>Content and editorial purpose</h3><p>Our services publish news, articles, commentary, features and other information for general information. We aim for accuracy, but news can develop and information may change after publication. We may update, correct, remove or reorganize content without prior notice.</p><h3>Acceptable use</h3><ul><li>Do not use our services for unlawful, abusive, defamatory, fraudulent or harmful activity.</li><li>Do not attempt unauthorized access, disrupt service availability, introduce malware or interfere with security.</li><li>Do not scrape, reproduce, republish or commercially exploit content except as permitted by law or with written permission.</li><li>Do not impersonate another person or submit misleading, infringing or malicious material.</li></ul><h3>User submissions</h3><p>You are responsible for material you submit. Do not submit confidential, unlawful or third-party personal information without authority. By submitting material, you confirm that you have the necessary rights and grant us permission to use it to review, display or respond to your submission in connection with the service, subject to applicable law.</p><h3>Availability and changes</h3><p>We may modify, suspend or discontinue any feature for maintenance, security, business or legal reasons. We do not guarantee uninterrupted or error-free availability.</p><h3>Third-party services</h3><p>Links, advertisements, embedded media and third-party services are provided for convenience. We do not control and are not responsible for third-party content, products, services or policies.</p></section>
<section class="section" id="disclaimer"><h2><span class="num">05</span>Disclaimer</h2><p>NEWSKERALA.NET provides content for general news and informational purposes. Unless expressly stated otherwise, content is not professional, legal, medical, financial or other specialist advice. Readers should independently verify important information and seek qualified advice where appropriate.</p><p>We make reasonable efforts to check information before publication, but do not warrant that all content is complete, current, accurate or suitable for every purpose. To the extent permitted by applicable law, we disclaim liability for loss arising from reliance on website, app or Telegram content, service interruptions, third-party websites or user-generated submissions.</p><p>Opinions expressed by contributors or quoted sources are their own and do not necessarily represent the views of NEWSKERALA.NET. Errors or concerns can be reported through the contact details below.</p></section>
<section class="section" id="cookies"><h2><span class="num">06</span>Cookie Policy</h2><p>Cookies and similar technologies may be used to keep the website working, remember preferences, understand traffic and support advertising where enabled.</p><div class="grid"><div class="tile"><b>Essential</b><span>Support core functions, security and navigation.</span></div><div class="tile"><b>Preferences</b><span>Remember settings such as language or display choices.</span></div><div class="tile"><b>Analytics</b><span>Help measure visits and understand how pages are used, if analytics is enabled.</span></div><div class="tile"><b>Advertising</b><span>May support ad delivery and measurement where advertising partners are enabled.</span></div></div><p>You can manage cookies through your browser settings. Blocking some cookies may affect website functionality. Where consent is legally required, non-essential cookies should not be activated before consent.</p></section>
<section class="section" id="copyright"><h2><span class="num">07</span>Copyright &amp; Content Policy</h2><p>Unless otherwise stated, original text, graphics, branding, logos, design elements and other material created for NEWSKERALA.NET are protected by applicable intellectual property laws. All rights are reserved.</p><p>News facts and ideas are not owned by us, but articles, photographs, videos, illustrations and other creative works may be protected by copyright. Third-party material remains the property of its respective owners and is used only where we believe we have permission, a licence or another lawful basis.</p><h3>Permitted sharing</h3><p>You may share links to our articles for personal, non-commercial purposes. Do not copy or republish full articles, photographs, videos or other protected material without permission, except where permitted by law.</p><h3>Copyright complaints</h3><p>If you believe material on our services infringes your copyright, send a notice identifying the work, the exact URL or location of the material, your contact details, a statement of your rights and a good-faith statement explaining the alleged infringement. We may request further information before taking action.</p></section>
<section class="section" id="rights"><h2><span class="num">08</span>Your Privacy Rights &amp; Choices</h2><p>Depending on your location and applicable law, you may have rights to request access to, correction of, deletion of or information about the processing of your personal data, and to withdraw consent or raise a complaint. These rights may be subject to identity verification, legal exceptions and other limitations.</p><ul><li>Use device settings to manage app permissions and notifications.</li><li>Use browser settings to manage cookies.</li><li>Use Telegram controls to stop or block bot messages.</li><li>Contact us to submit a privacy request or complaint.</li></ul><p>We will review and respond to valid requests within the time required by applicable law.</p></section>
<section class="section" id="contact"><h2><span class="num">09</span>Contact &amp; Privacy Complaints</h2><p>For privacy questions, correction or deletion requests, copyright complaints, or other policy-related concerns, contact the NEWSKERALA.NET team:</p><div class="contact"><span><b>Website:</b> <a href="https://newskerala.net">newskerala.net</a></span><span><b>Email:</b> <span class="placeholder">REPLACE_WITH_OFFICIAL_EMAIL</span></span><span><b>Publisher / Legal Entity:</b> <span class="placeholder">ADD_LEGAL_PUBLISHER_NAME</span></span></div><div class="notice"><b>Before publishing:</b> Replace the highlighted placeholders with a monitored official email and the correct publisher/legal entity. Add the names and store links of each app. Confirm the actual analytics, advertising, cookies, SDKs, bot logging, account features and retention periods used in production. Remove any statement that does not match your real implementation.</div><h3>Changes to these policies</h3><p>We may revise these policies as our services or legal requirements change. The updated version will be posted on this page with a revised effective date. Continued use after an update means you acknowledge the updated notice, to the extent permitted by law.</p></section>
